  "body": "## What changed\n\n`post --machine <file>` (`crates/post/src/bin/post.rs`) handed the engine the raw `.mch` JSON. `script_props` reads only the static grammar (`kinematics.static.*`), and every shipped machine is a vendor kinematics tree (`kinematics.default.parts`). So the CLI script saw no rotaries, no spindle max, no coolant codes and no rates.\n\nThe binary now posts a vendor tree with `post::machine::mirror(parse_mch(..))`, the same value the app hands the engine (`posting_mounts::machine_value_for`). It calls this through a small `script_machine` helper. The mirror already lives in camcraft-post, so no new crate edge is added.\n\n- A static-grammar file (no `kinematics.default.parts`) still posts exactly as written. Mirroring it would empty it.\n- The raw-file refusals run first and are unchanged: the parse errors and `inverted_post_refusal` (inverted Z or a letter other than X/Y).\n- The mirror carries the file's inverted axes as `invertedAxes`, computed by the same `Machine::inverted_axes`, so `invert::apply` mirrors or refuses an inverted X/Y the same way it did before.\n\nDecisions are recorded in `docs/decisions/996-cli-post-mirrored-machine.md`.\n\n## Before / after\n\n- **Before:** `post --machine assets/machines/tilthead.mch fanuc.cps <tilted stream>` warned \"tilted move on a machine without a tilting rotary\" and wrote no angle words. On `vmc.mch`, a 20000 rpm stream gave no spindle warning, and a mist op got no M7.\n- **After:** tilthead posts G43.4 with A/B words and M8, with no warnings. vmc warns \"spindle rpm over machine maximum\" at 20000 rpm (max 12000) and posts M7 for mist. In both cases the CLI's program is byte-equal to `engine::run(cps, mirror(parse_mch(file)), stream)`, the app's program.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New suite `crates/post/tests/vendor_mch_cli.rs`:\n  - `the_cli_posts_a_tilted_stream_on_the_shipped_tilthead`\n  - `the_cli_holds_a_shipped_machines_spindle_max_and_coolant_codes`\n\n  Both fail on the old binary and pass on this head.\n- The existing `axis_direction_cli` tests still pass: inverted X mirrored, inverted Z refused by name, unverified script refused.\n- I ran every `crates/post/tests` suite by hand (post_engine, axis_direction_cli, comp, comp_plane, mch_head_search, vendor_mch_cli), plus `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` and the full `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- I only checked the Fanuc post through the CLI on vendor files. The other scripts read the same `machine` global the app already feeds them.\n- I did not compare the CLI against the app on a `.mch` whose default holder the holder library would refuse. The CLI keeps the word-only reader, because camcraft-post does not depend on camcraft-tools. That check only refuses and never changes a posted word.\n\n## Follow-up\n\nThe #926 recorded runner (`crates/post/tests/recorded/mod.rs`, PR #1002, also edited on #994's branch) works around this bug by mirroring the machine itself. That file is left untouched here so the stacks don't conflict. Once #1002 merges, the runner can pass the `.mch` file straight through to the CLI.\n\nChangelog: The command-line post now reads a vendor `.mch` the way the app does, so its rotaries, spindle maximum and coolant codes reach the script (no false \"machine without a tilting rotary\" refusal on tilthead.mch).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at v0.17.0.\n\nFixes #996\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
